#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Considerations for setting up IBM Quantum Platform in an organization"
msgstr "Mga konsiderasyon sa pag-set up ng IBM Quantum Platform sa isang organisasyon"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Considerations for setting up IBM Quantum Platform for an organization"
msgstr "Mga konsiderasyon sa pag-set up ng IBM Quantum Platform para sa isang organisasyon"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore chemlab */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore chemlab */}\n"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Considerations for setting up IBM Quantum Platform for an organization {#considerations-for-setting-up-ibm-quantum-platform-for-an-organization}"
msgstr "Mga konsiderasyon sa pag-set up ng IBM Quantum Platform para sa isang organisasyon {#considerations-for-setting-up-ibm-quantum-platform-for-an-organization}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM Quantum&reg; Platform is the dashboard for your IBM Cloud&reg; account's IBM Quantum Compute Service instances and workloads, and provides a simplified view of access management. An organization's IBM Cloud account can have multiple users and multiple Quantum Compute instances, each with its own allocation. Identity and Access Management (IAM) controls which users can access which service instances, so you can enable collaboration while restricting visibility where needed. Access management becomes more relevant if you have service instances on paid plans. See [IBM Cloud account structure](/guides/cloud-account-structure) for an overview of how accounts, users, instances, and access fit together. Refer to the [IBM Cloud IAM documentation](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/account?topic=account-iamoverview) for full details on the IAM concepts referenced in this guide, such as access groups, policies, roles, and resource groups.\n"
msgstr "Ang IBM Quantum&reg; Platform ay ang dashboard para sa mga instance at workload ng IBM Quantum Compute Service ng iyong IBM Cloud&reg; account, at nagbibigay ng pinasimpleng view ng access management. Ang IBM Cloud account ng isang organisasyon ay maaaring magkaroon ng maraming user at maraming Quantum Compute instance, bawat isa ay may sariling allocation. Kinokontrol ng Identity and Access Management (IAM) kung aling mga user ang maaaring mag-access sa aling mga service instance, kaya maaari kang magbigay-daan sa collaboration habang nirerestrict ang visibility kung saan kailangan. Nagiging mas relevant ang access management kung mayroon kang mga service instance sa mga bayad na plano. Tingnan ang [IBM Cloud account structure](/guides/cloud-account-structure) para sa isang overview kung paano magkasama ang mga account, user, instance, at access. Sumangguni sa [IBM Cloud IAM documentation](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/account?topic=account-iamoverview) para sa buong detalye ng mga konsepto ng IAM na binanggit sa gabay na ito, tulad ng access groups, policies, roles, at resource groups.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide describes the decisions and tradeoffs involved in setting up access for an organization with multiple service instances &mdash; for example, assigning one instance per team or workload.\n"
msgstr "Inilalarawan ng gabay na ito ang mga desisyon at tradeoffs na kaugnay sa pag-set up ng access para sa isang organisasyon na may maraming service instance &mdash; halimbawa, ang pag-assign ng isang instance kada team o workload.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"If your organization has multiple IBM Cloud accounts &mdash; for example, separate accounts per business unit, each with its own Quantum Compute instances &mdash; you can link them under a single IBM Cloud Enterprise account, which has one main account responsible for billing and one or more child accounts. To redistribute Premium or Flex Plan allocation between child accounts, contact IBM Quantum support through the [IBM Cloud Support Center](https://cloud.ibm.com/unifiedsupport/cases/form). See the [IBM Cloud Enterprise account documentation](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/account?topic=account-what-is-enterprise) for full details.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"overview-org\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"overview-org\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview {#overview}"
msgstr "Pangkalahatang-ideya {#overview}"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid ""
#| "   <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
#| "   IBM Cloud&reg; provides various ways to implement these mechanisms described in this guide. There are several ways to achieve these objectives. Additionally, most of the steps in this guide are generic to IBM Cloud and not specific to IBM Quantum Platform, except the custom role details.\n"
#| "</Admonition>\n"
msgid ""
"   <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"   IBM Cloud&reg; provides several ways to implement the mechanisms described in this guide. Most of the steps are generic to IBM Cloud and not specific to Quantum Compute, except the custom role details.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"   <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"   Ang IBM Cloud&reg; ay nagbibigay ng iba't ibang paraan upang ipatupad ang mga mekanismong inilarawan sa gabay na ito. Mayroon ding ilang paraan upang makamit ang mga layuning ito. Bukod dito, karamihan sa mga hakbang sa gabay na ito ay pangkalahatang para sa IBM Cloud at hindi partikular sa IBM Quantum Platform, maliban sa mga detalye ng custom role.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Involved personas {#involved-personas}"
msgstr "Mga taong kasangkot {#involved-personas}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following personas are mentioned in this guide:\n"
msgstr "Ang mga sumusunod na persona ay binabanggit sa gabay na ito:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**User**: Someone who gets access to Quantum Compute resources (_service instances_) and can potentially collaborate with other users on these resources. Users' access is controlled by an administrator, and they cannot create or delete service instances.\n"
msgstr "**User**: Isang taong nakakakuha ng access sa Quantum Compute resources (_service instances_) at maaaring makipagtulungan sa ibang mga gumagamit sa mga resource na ito. Ang access ng mga gumagamit ay kontrolado ng isang administrator, at hindi sila maaaring lumikha o magtanggal ng mga service instance.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Cloud administrator**: An IBM Cloud account owner who owns IBM Quantum Compute resources and manages which users can access these resources. As the resource owner, the administrator is charged for any paid resource use.\n"
msgstr "**Cloud administrator**: Isang IBM Cloud account owner na nagmamay-ari ng IBM Quantum Compute resources at namamahala kung sino ang may access sa mga resource na ito. Bilang may-ari ng resource, ang administrator ay sisingilin para sa anumang bayad na paggamit ng resource.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**IDP administrator**: An administrator who defines identities and their attributes in an identity provider (IDP).\n"
msgstr "**IDP administrator**: Isang administrator na nagtatakda ng mga pagkakakilanlan at ang kanilang mga katangian sa isang identity provider (IDP).\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Terminology {#terminology}"
msgstr "Terminolohiya {#terminology}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide uses the following terms:\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ng gabay na ito ang mga sumusunod na termino:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "_Resource_: A generic IBM Cloud term that refers to an object that can be managed through the Cloud user interface, CLI, or API. For this guide, a _resource_ is a Quantum Compute Service instance.\n"
msgstr "_Resource_: Isang pangkaraniwang IBM Cloud term na tumutukoy sa isang object na maaaring pamahalaan sa pamamagitan ng Cloud user interface, CLI, o API. Para sa gabay na ito, ang _resource_ ay isang Quantum Compute Service instance.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "_Service instance_: A service instance is used to access Cloud services - specifically, quantum computers, through IBM Quantum Compute Service. It is defined through the catalog. You can define several service instances based on the same or different plans, which offer access to different quantum computing backends. See [Available IBM Cloud plans](/guides/plans-overview) for details.\n"
msgstr "_Service instance_: Ang isang service instance ay ginagamit para ma-access ang mga Cloud service — partikular, ang mga quantum computer, sa pamamagitan ng IBM Quantum Compute Service. Ito ay tinukoy sa pamamagitan ng catalog. Maaari kang magtukoy ng maraming service instance batay sa parehong o iba't ibang plano, na nag-aalok ng access sa iba't ibang quantum computing backend. Tingnan ang [Available IBM Cloud plans](/guides/plans-overview) para sa mga detalye.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"xplanning-orgx\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"xplanning-orgx\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plan your setup {#plan-your-setup}"
msgstr "Planuhin ang iyong setup {#plan-your-setup}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before you set up IBM Quantum Platform for your organization, you need to make these decisions:\n"
msgstr "Bago mo i-set up ang IBM Quantum Platform para sa iyong organisasyon, kailangan mong gawin ang mga desisyong ito:\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**How are user identities defined?** You can set up IBM Cloud users, users from another identity provider (IDP), or both.\n"
msgstr "**Paano tinutukoy ang mga pagkakakilanlan ng gumagamit?** Maaari kang mag-set up ng mga IBM Cloud user, mga gumagamit mula sa ibang identity provider (IDP), o pareho.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you are using a different IDP, does the Cloud administrator or the IDP administrator assign users to access groups?\n"
msgstr "Kung gumagamit ka ng ibang IDP, ang Cloud administrator o ang IDP administrator ba ang nag-aasign ng mga gumagamit sa mga access group?\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the IDP administrator assigns users through dynamic rules, you need a custom IDP user attribute to use as a matching key (for example, a `team` attribute).\n"
msgstr "Kung ita-assign ng IDP administrator ang mga user sa pamamagitan ng dynamic rules, kakailanganin mo ng custom na IDP user attribute upang gamitin bilang matching key (halimbawa, isang `team` attribute).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**How many service instances do you need, and what will each be used for?** Plan your instance names carefully. Whenever you create a service instance through the IBM Quantum Platform user interface, the platform makes an additional call to IAM on your behalf to create a matching access group (with the same name as the instance, with \"Collaborators\" appended) that grants write access to that instance.  Therefore, instance names become access group names too. This extra step only happens when you create an instance through the IBM Quantum Platform user interface. It does not happen if you create the instance by using Terraform, the IBM Cloud CLI, or the IBM Cloud API.\n"
msgstr "**Ilang service instance ang kailangan mo, at para saan gagamitin ang bawat isa?** Planuhin nang mabuti ang mga pangalan ng iyong instance. Tuwing gagawa ka ng service instance sa pamamagitan ng IBM Quantum Platform user interface, ang platform ay gumagawa ng karagdagang tawag sa IAM sa iyong ngalan upang gumawa ng katumbas na access group (na may parehong pangalan ng instance, na may \"Collaborators\" na idinagdag) na nagbibigay ng write access sa instance na iyon. Kaya, ang mga pangalan ng instance ay nagiging mga pangalan ng access group din. Ang karagdagang hakbang na ito ay nangyayari lamang kapag gumawa ka ng instance sa pamamagitan ng IBM Quantum Platform user interface. Hindi ito nangyayari kung gagawa ka ng instance gamit ang Terraform, ang IBM Cloud CLI, o ang IBM Cloud API.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Workloads belong to service instances, and users who have access to an instance can see its workloads.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga workload ay kabilang sa mga service instance, at ang mga user na may access sa isang instance ay makakakita ng mga workload nito.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Service instances can be based on different plans, allowing access to different backends and allocations.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga service instance ay maaaring nakabatay sa iba't ibang plano, na nagbibigay ng access sa iba't ibang backend at allocations.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Which users need to access which service instances?**\n"
msgstr "**Aling mga user ang kailangan mag-access sa aling mga service instance?**\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Should users be able to delete workloads?** Keeping workloads in service instances gives more traceability for billing costs.\n"
msgstr "**Dapat bang makapag-delete ng workloads ang mga gumagamit?** Ang pagpapanatili ng mga workload sa mga service instance ay nagbibigay ng mas maraming traceability para sa mga gastos sa billing.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Will you use the access group that's automatically created for each instance, create additional access groups of your own, assign access to individual users directly, or organize instances into resource groups?**\n"
msgstr "**Gagamitin mo ba ang access group na awtomatikong nagagawa para sa bawat instance, gagawa ng karagdagang mga access group na sarili mo, direktang mag-a-assign ng access sa indibidwal na mga user, o oorganisahin ang mga instance sa mga resource groups?**\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Access groups** are a convenient and common way of controlling user access to IBM Cloud resources. Every service instance you create through the IBM Quantum Platform user interface already has its own \"Collaborators\" access group. You can use that group as-is, or create additional access groups in the IBM Cloud console to group users by team or workload (for example, `ml` and `finance`) across one or more instances. Each access group uses a custom role that allows users to access specific service instances or resource groups. If you don't need a group of users to share the same access, you can also assign access to individual users directly, without an access group.\n"
msgstr "**Ang mga access group** ay isang maginhawa at karaniwang paraan ng pagkontrol sa user access sa mga resource ng IBM Cloud. Ang bawat service instance na ginawa mo sa pamamagitan ng IBM Quantum Platform user interface ay mayroon nang sariling \"Collaborators\" access group. Maaari mong gamitin ang group na iyon as-is, o gumawa ng karagdagang mga access group sa IBM Cloud console upang pangkatin ang mga user ayon sa team o workload (halimbawa, `ml` at `finance`) sa isa o higit pang mga instance. Ang bawat access group ay gumagamit ng custom role na nagpapahintulot sa mga user na mag-access ng mga tiyak na service instance o resource groups. Kung hindi mo kailangan ng isang grupo ng mga user na magbahagi ng parehong access, maaari mo ring direktang i-assign ang access sa indibidwal na mga user, nang walang access group.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '      * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you use dynamic rules based on IDP attributes to assign users to access groups, avoid attribute values that are substrings of one another. For example, if you use `ml` and `chemlab` as attribute values, a rule matching `ml` would also match `chemlab`, accidentally granting more access than expected. Use unique values such as `ml` and `chem-lab`, or add prefixes or suffixes to avoid unintended substring matches.\n"
msgstr "Kung gagamit ka ng dynamic rules batay sa IDP attributes upang i-assign ang mga user sa mga access group, iwasan ang mga attribute value na substring ng isa't isa. Halimbawa, kung gagamitin mo ang `ml` at `chemlab` bilang mga attribute value, ang isang rule na tumutugma sa `ml` ay tutugma rin sa `chemlab`, na hindi sinasadyang nagbibigay ng mas maraming access kaysa inaasahan. Gumamit ng natatanging mga halaga tulad ng `ml` at `chem-lab`, o magdagdag ng mga prefix o suffix upang maiwasan ang hindi sinasadyang substring match.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Resource groups** are used only when you need to maintain a clear separation of service instances. When creating a service instance from IBM Quantum Platform, you can select which resource group it belongs to (and add tags), but you must use the IBM Cloud console to create or manage the resource groups. If more service instances are created in a resource group, all users who have access to the resource group see them automatically, without updating access groups. If you choose to use resource groups, first create access groups and then assign them to resource groups.\n"
msgstr "**Ang mga resource group** ay ginagamit lamang kapag kailangan mong mapanatili ang malinaw na paghihiwalay ng mga service instance. Kapag gumagawa ng service instance mula sa IBM Quantum Platform, maaari mong piliin kung aling resource group ito kabilang (at magdagdag ng tags), ngunit kailangan mong gamitin ang IBM Cloud console upang gumawa o mamahala ng mga resource group. Kung mas maraming service instance ang nilikha sa isang resource group, lahat ng user na may access sa resource group ay awtomatikong makakakita ng mga ito, nang hindi kina-update ang mga access group. Kung pipiliin mong gumamit ng mga resource group, una gumawa ka ng mga access group at pagkatapos ay i-aassign ang mga ito sa mga resource group.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid ""
#| "   <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
#| "   A service instance can belong to only one resource group. After instances are assigned into resource groups, they cannot be changed. This also means that the resource group assignment can  happen only at service instance creation. Therefore, resource groups might not provide enough flexibility if assignments of service instances to resource groups might need to change.\n"
#| "   </Admonition>\n"
msgid ""
"   <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"   A service instance can belong to only one resource group, and that assignment cannot be changed after the instance is created. Therefore, resource groups might not provide enough flexibility if service instances might need to move between resource groups later.\n"
"   </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"   <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"   Ang isang service instance ay maaaring kabilang sa isang resource group lamang. Pagkatapos na ma-assign ang mga instance sa mga resource group, hindi na ito maaaring baguhin. Nangangahulugan din ito na ang pag-aasign ng resource group ay maaari lamang mangyari sa paglikha ng service instance. Kaya naman, ang mga resource group ay maaaring hindi magbigay ng sapat na flexibility kung ang mga pag-aasign ng mga service instance sa mga resource group ay maaaring kailangang baguhin.\n"
"   </Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Considerations {#considerations}"
msgstr "Mga konsiderasyon {#considerations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You should understand the following considerations when setting up your environment.\n"
msgstr "Dapat mong maunawaan ang mga sumusunod na konsiderasyon kapag nag-set up ng iyong kapaligiran.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define more fine-grained roles {#define-more-fine-grained-roles}"
msgstr "Tukuyin ang mas detalyadong mga role {#define-more-fine-grained-roles}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Custom roles can be used for more fine-grained access control. For example, some users might need full access to work on service instances, while others might only need read access to service instances, programs, and workloads.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga aksyon sa mga custom role ay maaaring gamitin para sa mas detalyadong access control. Halimbawa, ang ilang mga gumagamit ay maaaring kailangan ng buong access para magtrabaho sa mga service instance, habang ang iba ay maaaring kailangan lamang ng read access sa mga service instance, program, at workload.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To achieve that, define two different custom roles, such as `MLreader` and `MLwriter`. Remove all cancel, delete, and update actions from the `MLreader` custom role, and include all actions in the `MLwriter` custom role. Then add the roles to two different access groups accordingly.\n"
msgstr "Upang makamit iyon, tukuyin ang dalawang iba't ibang custom role, tulad ng `MLreader` at `MLwriter`. Alisin ang lahat ng cancel, delete, at update actions mula sa `MLreader` custom role, at isama ang lahat ng aksyon sa `MLwriter` custom role. Pagkatapos, idagdag ang mga role sa dalawang iba't ibang access group nang naaayon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid ""
#| "<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
#| "When using dynamic rules, that is, when the identity provider (IDP) administrator manages access through custom IDP user attributes, do not use IDP custom user attributes that are substrings of each other. For instance, don't use `ml` and `mlReader`, as the string comparison of `ml` would also accept `mlReader`. You could use `MLreader` and `MLwriter` to avoid this conflict.\n"
#| "</Admonition>\n"
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"When using dynamic rules, that is, when the IDP administrator manages access through custom IDP user attributes, do not use IDP custom user attributes that are substrings of each other. For instance, don't use `ml` and `mlReader`, as the string comparison of `ml` would also accept `mlReader`. You could use `MLreader` and `MLwriter` to avoid this conflict.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Kapag gumagamit ng mga dynamic rule, iyon ay, kapag ang identity provider (IDP) administrator ay namamahala ng access sa pamamagitan ng mga custom IDP user attribute, huwag gumamit ng mga IDP custom user attribute na mga substring ng isa't isa. Halimbawa, huwag gumamit ng `ml` at `mlReader`, dahil ang string comparison ng `ml` ay tatanggap din ng `mlReader`. Maaari kang gumamit ng `MLreader` at `MLwriter` upang maiwasan ang salungatan na ito.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For an example, see [Set up custom roles](/guides/custom-roles#custom).\n"
msgstr "Para sa isang halimbawa, tingnan ang [Set up custom roles](/guides/custom-roles#custom).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"shared-access\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"shared-access\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shared workload access {#shared-workload-access}"
msgstr "Access sa shared workload {#shared-workload-access}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Access applies to service instances. Thus, users with write access to an instance (including through the \"Collaborators\" access group automatically created for instances made by the IBM Quantum Platform user interface) can cancel their own workloads, but can also view and cancel other users' workloads in that instance. This is a function of how IAM works and cannot be changed.\n"
msgstr "Ang access ay nalalapat sa mga service instance. Kaya naman, ang mga gumagamit na may write access sa isang instance (kabilang ang sa pamamagitan ng \"Collaborators\" access group na awtomatikong ginagawa para sa mga instance na nilikha ng IBM Quantum Platform user interface) ay maaaring kanselahin ang kanilang sariling mga workload, ngunit maaari rin nilang tingnan at kanselahin ang mga workload ng ibang gumagamit sa instance na iyon. Ito ay isang function ng kung paano gumagana ang IAM at hindi maaaring baguhin.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"nest-org\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"nest-org\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulate hierarchical structures {#simulate-hierarchical-structures}"
msgstr "Gayahin ang mga hierarchical na istruktura {#simulate-hierarchical-structures}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By default, each service instance's access is managed independently, for example, through the \"Collaborators\" access group automatically created for instances that were made through the IBM Quantum Platform user interface. IAM doesn't have a built-in hierarchy of groups, but you can approximate one by creating access groups that reference multiple teams' service instances. Users who need broad access only need to be added to one \"top level\" group, instead of to each team's individual access group.\n"
msgstr "Bilang default, ang access ng bawat service instance ay pinamamahalaan nang hiwalay, halimbawa, sa pamamagitan ng \"Collaborators\" access group na awtomatikong ginagawa para sa mga instance na nilikha sa pamamagitan ng IBM Quantum Platform user interface. Walang built-in na hierarchy ng mga grupo ang IAM, ngunit maaari kang gumawa ng katulad nito sa pamamagitan ng paglikha ng mga access group na tumutukoy sa mga service instance ng maraming team. Ang mga gumagamit na nangangailangan ng malawak na access ay kailangan lamang idagdag sa isang \"top level\" na grupo, sa halip na sa bawat indibidwal na access group ng bawat team.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"repeat-org\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"repeat-org\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consistent and repeatable deployment of the configuration {#consistent-and-repeatable-deployment-of-the-configuration}"
msgstr "Pare-pareho at paulit-ulit na pag-deploy ng configuration {#consistent-and-repeatable-deployment-of-the-configuration}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The steps in this guide can be automated for consistent and repeatable management of users, service instances, and the access mappings between them. Refer to the [Terraform IBM Cloud&reg; Provider documentation](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/IBM-Cloud/ibm/latest/docs) for templates.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga hakbang sa gabay na ito ay maaaring i-automate para sa pare-pareho at paulit-ulit na pamamahala ng mga gumagamit, mga service instance, at ang access mappings sa pagitan ng mga ito. Sumangguni sa [Terraform IBM Cloud&reg; Provider documentation](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/IBM-Cloud/ibm/latest/docs) para sa mga template.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can use Terraform to set allocation and limits, as well as restrict backend access, for `quantum-computing` service instances. See [Getting started with Terraform on IBM Cloud](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/ibm-cloud-provider-for-terraform?topic=ibm-cloud-provider-for-terraform-getting-started) for more information.\n"
msgstr "Maaari mong gamitin ang Terraform para itakda ang allocation at mga limitasyon, pati na rin ang paghigpit sa backend access, para sa mga `quantum-computing` service instance. Tingnan ang [Getting started with Terraform on IBM Cloud](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/ibm-cloud-provider-for-terraform?topic=ibm-cloud-provider-for-terraform-getting-started) para sa karagdagang impormasyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example:\n"
msgstr "Halimbawa:\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Mga susunod na hakbang {#next-steps}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"   * See [Configure IBM Quantum Platform for an organization](/guides/quickstart-steps-org) for the steps to set up IBM Quantum Platform.\n"
"   * [Understand available plans](/guides/plans-overview).\n"
"   * [Create instances](/guides/instances).\n"
